WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:08.010
Long ago, an astrologer looked up, and glimpsed
the primeval current in the sky above.

00:00:08.010 --> 00:00:13.809
Then, miraculously, what they saw in the cosmos
actually manifested in reality - and the very

00:00:13.809 --> 00:00:17.770
amber of the stars rained down on the Lands
Between.

00:00:17.770 --> 00:00:23.290
This glintstone of the cosmos would go on
to inspire those that studied it - but there

00:00:23.290 --> 00:00:26.830
was also a darkness up there, between the
stars.

00:00:26.830 --> 00:00:33.100
And what some saw, would break their minds..and
inspire a fate worse than death.

00:00:33.100 --> 00:00:36.600
This is the story of Elden Ring's Cosmic Sorcery.

00:00:36.600 --> 00:00:40.770
A force that would define an entire era of
life, in the Lands Between

00:00:40.770 --> 00:00:56.180
---

00:00:56.180 --> 00:01:01.520
It all began with the "Founding Rain of Stars",
a legendary sorcery that was the "founding

00:01:01.520 --> 00:01:03.239
glintstone sorcery" [Source: Founding Rain
of Stars].

00:01:03.239 --> 00:01:08.630
You might have missed this spell in your playthrough
- but it's located here, hidden along an illusory

00:01:08.630 --> 00:01:14.009
path leading to the Heretical Rise, within
the Mountaintops of the Giants.

00:01:14.009 --> 00:01:19.840
Its description reveals that it is "the eldest
primeval sorcery, said to have been discovered

00:01:19.840 --> 00:01:21.450
by an ancient astrologer".

00:01:21.450 --> 00:01:24.420
Now..we don't know who this astrologer was.

00:01:24.420 --> 00:01:26.470
But we know he was not alone.

00:01:26.470 --> 00:01:32.690
For it was here, in these icy peaks closest
to the sky, that the "Astrologers, who preceded

00:01:32.690 --> 00:01:35.770
the sorcerers, established themselves" [Source:
Sword of Night and Flame].

00:01:35.770 --> 00:01:40.500
And with ancient tools of astronomy, they
looked to the cosmos above, and read fate

00:01:40.500 --> 00:01:41.630
in the stars [Source: Astrologer's Robe].

00:01:41.630 --> 00:01:47.300
But this was more than mere stargazing - the
stars quite literally govern fates in Elden

00:01:47.300 --> 00:01:48.300
Ring.

00:01:48.300 --> 00:01:52.440
We learn this from the Starlight Shards and
Amber Starlight items.

00:01:52.440 --> 00:01:57.860
The former is a pale blue shard - what remains
of a passing flash of starlight [Source: Starlight

00:01:57.860 --> 00:02:03.219
Shard], and the latter is the same, except
with a pale amber glow, and it tells of the

00:02:03.219 --> 00:02:09.509
belief that "if the stars command our fates,
then amber-hued stars must command the fates

00:02:09.509 --> 00:02:11.069
of the gods".

00:02:11.069 --> 00:02:16.670
During Seluvis's questline, the blue starlight
shards are distilled into a blue tonic, which

00:02:16.670 --> 00:02:21.150
can be given to other NPCs to turn them into
summonable puppets.

00:02:21.150 --> 00:02:27.780
You are..quite literally using starlight to
forcibly control and take away their fates,

00:02:27.780 --> 00:02:29.269
when you do this.

00:02:29.269 --> 00:02:34.580
These same "intoxicating draughts" had historically
been used in the Eternal City [Source: Starlight

00:02:34.580 --> 00:02:40.840
Shard], as is exemplified by the Nightmaiden
&amp; Swordstress Puppets, who chose this controlled

00:02:40.840 --> 00:02:46.970
fate for themselves, presumably to better
serve the needs of the Eternal City.

00:02:46.970 --> 00:02:52.390
You can learn more about that in this video,
where we discuss the Eternal City in its entirety.

00:02:52.390 --> 00:02:58.480
But the Nox of the Eternal City weren't the
only ones that drew power from the stars.

00:02:58.480 --> 00:03:02.920
The Royal House of Caria too, drew great power
from Astrology.

00:03:02.920 --> 00:03:10.849
The Telescope specifically is a small part
of a larger "astrological tool" that was "used

00:03:10.849 --> 00:03:16.549
by members of the Carian Royal Family", for
their own brand of "Carian astrology" that

00:03:16.549 --> 00:03:19.819
revolved around Rennala, and the Full Moon.

00:03:19.819 --> 00:03:26.720
But to most, the moon was not considered equal
to the stars - and it was the stars that most

00:03:26.720 --> 00:03:29.069
would draw upon for their sorcery.

00:03:29.069 --> 00:03:35.230
These sorcerers would come together at Raya
Lucaria, a place of learning, that institutionalised

00:03:35.230 --> 00:03:38.290
the practice of glintstone sorcery.

00:03:38.290 --> 00:03:42.690
And this is our little triumvirate of three
factions.

00:03:42.690 --> 00:03:50.980
The Nox, the Carians, and the sorcerers of
Raya Lucaria - who all trace their origins

00:03:50.980 --> 00:03:52.890
back to astrology.

00:03:52.890 --> 00:03:59.230
They overlap at times, they interact, and
clash, and their shared history is fascinating..and

00:03:59.230 --> 00:04:09.690
complicated - but it all comes back to the
stars, in the end.

00:04:09.690 --> 00:04:10.690
---

00:04:10.690 --> 00:04:14.890
But let's return once again to the "Founding
Rain of Stars", which tells us that "the glimpse

00:04:14.890 --> 00:04:20.489
of the primeval current that the (ancient)
astrologer saw became a reality, and the stars'

00:04:20.489 --> 00:04:22.240
amber rained down on this land".

00:04:22.240 --> 00:04:23.419
[Source: JP Founding Rain of Stars].

00:04:23.419 --> 00:04:26.060
But: what exactly is the primeval current?

00:04:26.060 --> 00:04:27.970
Well, let's break down the term.

00:04:27.970 --> 00:04:32.340
The word "current" means it's a moving "flow"
, or a "torrent" [Source: Comet Azur], and

00:04:32.340 --> 00:04:38.350
the word "primeval" means that this "torrential
flow" likely existed from the very beginning

00:04:38.350 --> 00:04:39.540
of time.

00:04:39.540 --> 00:04:45.270
And thanks to the description for Comet Azur,
we know that the primeval current is a "distant

00:04:45.270 --> 00:04:50.830
starry expanse", something that is visually
similar to the torrential comet generated

00:04:50.830 --> 00:04:52.440
from this spell.

00:04:52.440 --> 00:04:57.850
But what's truly amazing about this cosmic
force, is that, somehow, this ancient astrologer

00:04:57.850 --> 00:05:04.500
managed to manifest a rain of stars upon the
earth, merely after glimpsing it in the primeval

00:05:04.500 --> 00:05:06.550
current of the cosmos, far away.

00:05:06.550 --> 00:05:11.120
And I speculate that Starlight Shards are
actually another example of this phenomenon.

00:05:11.120 --> 00:05:15.712
Their description reveals that these are "what
remains of a passing flash of starlight" [Source:

00:05:15.712 --> 00:05:21.370
Starlight Shard], and we exclusively loot
these at the foot of giant stone astrolabes,

00:05:21.370 --> 00:05:24.160
which are these ancient stargazing tools [The
exception being the Cathedral of Manus Celes,

00:05:24.160 --> 00:05:25.160
which is itself built on a famous stargazing
field].

00:05:25.160 --> 00:05:29.940
Thus, rather than being a piece of a star
that has fallen to the ground, I think these

00:05:29.940 --> 00:05:34.430
might be a byproduct of the act of looking
up at the stars.

00:05:34.430 --> 00:05:36.000
Why else would we loot them here?

00:05:36.000 --> 00:05:41.290
And so, in that same manner first established
with Starlight Shards and the Founding Rain

00:05:41.290 --> 00:05:46.310
of Stars, Glintstone Sorcerers would go on
to replicate this phenomenon - using their

00:05:46.310 --> 00:05:48.770
powers of comprehension [Note: Intelligence
is "comprehension power" in JP] to conceive

00:05:48.770 --> 00:05:52.919
of new cosmic elements that could be manifested
in reality.

00:05:52.919 --> 00:05:58.800
Or, put another way, they formulated "spells"
that let them throw giant rocks at eachother,

00:05:58.800 --> 00:06:01.010
and it was a huge hit with everyone.

00:06:01.010 --> 00:06:06.720
But among these glintstone sorcerers were
some, who wished to truly understand the mysteries

00:06:06.720 --> 00:06:09.720
of the primeval current - no matter the cost.

00:06:09.720 --> 00:06:15.539
These were sorcerers like Lusat and Azur,
who would literally become crystal in order

00:06:15.539 --> 00:06:20.530
to sync up with and better understand these
powers of the cosmos.

00:06:20.530 --> 00:06:25.880
And then there was Sellen - the graven witch,
who threw all ethics to the wind, and wished

00:06:25.880 --> 00:06:29.580
to see humanity ascend - no matter the cost.

00:06:29.580 --> 00:06:33.000
For the stars..are alive.

00:06:33.000 --> 00:06:40.100
Look at Astel, for example - a malformed star,
but a star nonetheless - birthed from a void,

00:06:40.100 --> 00:06:41.850
or so it is said [Source: Remembrance of the
Naturalborn, Bastard's Stars].

00:06:41.850 --> 00:06:43.560
But I'm getting ahead of myself.

00:06:43.560 --> 00:06:48.510
Most sorcerers, however, would be content
with merely manifesting cosmic power.

00:06:48.510 --> 00:06:55.580
And so, they would embed physical glintstone
into a staff, and using it as a sort of catalyst

00:06:55.580 --> 00:06:57.169
for the stars above[Source: Astrologer's Staff,
Staff of Loss].

00:06:57.169 --> 00:07:03.050
You need such staffs to channel spells in
Elden Ring, and Sorcerers needed glintstone

00:07:03.050 --> 00:07:09.510
to study - thus,, having access to physical
glintstone was likely quite an important thing.

00:07:09.510 --> 00:07:14.729
And luckily for the sorcerers, Glintstone,
being sourced from comets and meteors, had

00:07:14.729 --> 00:07:17.330
fallen to the Lands Between before.

00:07:17.330 --> 00:07:21.449
So these valuable crystals were mined, and
put to great use.

00:07:21.449 --> 00:07:28.539
So, atop and amidst enormous quantities of
glintstone in the Lakes of Liurnia, a place

00:07:28.539 --> 00:07:30.470
of learning was built.

00:07:30.470 --> 00:07:35.900
An institution, known as the Raya Lucaria
Academy

00:07:35.900 --> 00:07:38.970
---
Sorcerers, as a whole.. were powerful.

00:07:38.970 --> 00:07:44.100
They could read fate in the stars, fire cosmic
projectiles at their enemies, and potentially

00:07:44.100 --> 00:07:46.110
even command the fates of others.

00:07:46.110 --> 00:07:50.169
So naturally, there needed to be an institution
for their power.

00:07:50.169 --> 00:07:56.620
A place of learning, but also a place of heirarchy,
and even governance, where rules about sorcery

00:07:56.620 --> 00:07:59.680
could be debated, and enforced.

00:07:59.680 --> 00:08:05.430
When you journeyed through Raya Lucaria, you
would have collected symbols of such a thing.

00:08:05.430 --> 00:08:09.230
These are stone masks, called "Glintstone
Crowns".

00:08:09.230 --> 00:08:12.120
And not just anyone is supposed to wear these
crowns.

00:08:12.120 --> 00:08:18.409
They're a symbol of achievement, and they
represent one's mastery of a certain conspectus,

00:08:18.409 --> 00:08:20.850
or school of learning, within the academy.

00:08:20.850 --> 00:08:21.850
[Source: Swift Glintstone Shard, Glintstone
Crowns].

00:08:21.850 --> 00:08:24.349
They also make a good weapon, if all else
fails.

00:08:24.349 --> 00:08:28.440
But why was this design specifically chosen
as a symbol of achievement?

00:08:28.440 --> 00:08:33.830
Well, according to many item descriptions
- there isn't just life in stone - but there

00:08:33.830 --> 00:08:36.430
is wisdom contained therein, as well.

00:08:36.430 --> 00:08:41.090
So, their masks were crafted of stone, and
set with glintstone.

00:08:41.090 --> 00:08:47.190
The glintstone is typically set upon the eyes,
and/or the brain, a tradition that I speculate

00:08:47.190 --> 00:08:53.120
originated with the sorcerer Azur, who was
one of the first, if not the first glintstone

00:08:53.120 --> 00:08:54.380
sorcerer.

00:08:54.380 --> 00:08:58.410
His blue-green glintstone crown [Source: Azur's
Glintstone Crown] was set with crystals, and

00:08:58.410 --> 00:09:04.370
eventually replaced his own brain and skull
altogether, which enhanced his powers by helping

00:09:04.370 --> 00:09:09.471
him catalyse with glintstone - though it clearly
came at great physical cost.

00:09:09.471 --> 00:09:10.471
[NOTE: This is reflected in the gameplay,
as all glintstone crowns increase the power

00:09:10.471 --> 00:09:11.471
of your sorceries, at the cost of another
attribute]

00:09:11.471 --> 00:09:17.220
And I specify that his crown eventually replaced
his own brain and skull, because glintstone

00:09:17.220 --> 00:09:18.220
does that.

00:09:18.220 --> 00:09:19.220
It corrodes.

00:09:19.220 --> 00:09:20.470
It consumes.

00:09:20.470 --> 00:09:26.089
We see its effects best on other creatures,
like the dragon Smarag, who was a devourer

00:09:26.089 --> 00:09:32.440
of sorcerers, with a body that become corroded
over time by glintstones, thanks to his strict

00:09:32.440 --> 00:09:33.779
sorcerer diet.

00:09:33.779 --> 00:09:38.990
But, as with Azur..this corrosion did not
come without benefits, and he now breathes

00:09:38.990 --> 00:09:41.709
a powerful glintstone breath.

00:09:41.709 --> 00:09:45.920
The sorcerer Azur was an early sorcerer of
the primeval current.

00:09:45.920 --> 00:09:47.579
But he wasn't the only one.

00:09:47.579 --> 00:09:53.640
There was also the sorcerer Lusat, who experienced
a similar glintstone convergence of body and

00:09:53.640 --> 00:09:54.640
mind.

00:09:54.640 --> 00:10:00.720
Together, these masters of sorcery each glimpsed
a part of the primeval current.

00:10:00.720 --> 00:10:05.730
And from what I gather, the primeval current
seems like the sort of thing that can only

00:10:05.730 --> 00:10:10.200
be glimpsed once, before it either breaks
or terrifies the viewer.

00:10:10.200 --> 00:10:16.079
Azur and Lusat only have one primeval current
spell each, after all.

00:10:16.079 --> 00:10:21.240
For instance, "When Lusat glimpsed into the
primeval current, he conceived of the spell

00:10:21.240 --> 00:10:28.110
"Stars of Ruin", and beheld the final moments
of a great star cluster, and upon seeing it,

00:10:28.110 --> 00:10:30.010
he too was broken" [Source: Stars of Ruin].

00:10:30.010 --> 00:10:33.770
And "when Azur glimpsed into the primeval
current, he saw darkness.

00:10:33.770 --> 00:10:35.570
He glimpsed beyond the wisdom of stone [Source:
Azur's Glintstone Staff], and conceived of

00:10:35.570 --> 00:10:40.800
the spell "Comet Azur", but was left both
bewitched and fearful of the abyss".

00:10:40.800 --> 00:10:46.700
Both Azur and Lusat clearly had a prominent
role at the Academy, but Azur specifically

00:10:46.700 --> 00:10:52.180
was the first founding glintstone sorcerer
to have an impact upon Raya Lucaria.

00:10:52.180 --> 00:10:57.779
For there is a line of research, called the
Karolos Conspectus, dubbed "The oldest of

00:10:57.779 --> 00:11:02.500
the academy's lineages of study, begat by
the sorcerer Azur" [Source: Karolos Glintstone

00:11:02.500 --> 00:11:03.500
Crown].

00:11:03.500 --> 00:11:08.620
Scholars who follow in his footsteps by studying
this conspectus pursue the mysteries of comets,

00:11:08.620 --> 00:11:14.200
leading to new kinds of comet sorceries like
Glintstone Cometshard, and Shard Spiral [Source:

00:11:14.200 --> 00:11:15.200
Shard Spiral, Comet, Glintstone Cometshard].

00:11:15.200 --> 00:11:19.240
Each conspectus appears to be named after
a founding individual.

00:11:19.240 --> 00:11:24.190
These stone crowns are designed after actual
people, after all - people you can see in

00:11:24.190 --> 00:11:27.970
the flesh, upon their matching portraits in
the academy.

00:11:27.970 --> 00:11:33.900
So even though the Karolos Conspectus follow
the path began by the sorcerer Azur [Source:

00:11:33.900 --> 00:11:39.500
Karolos Glintstone Crown] - their conspectus
of learning must have been formalised by someone

00:11:39.500 --> 00:11:40.570
named Karolos.

00:11:40.570 --> 00:11:47.060
But as time went on, more conspectus's needed
to be created, as new lines of inquiry were

00:11:47.060 --> 00:11:48.060
discovered.

00:11:48.060 --> 00:11:54.029
And so logically, the Olivinus Conspectus
should have been the second to be created.

00:11:54.029 --> 00:11:59.110
For this line of research is also concerned
with the study of meteors in the primeval

00:11:59.110 --> 00:12:03.840
current, except this conspectus "began with
the sorcerer Lusat".

00:12:03.840 --> 00:12:09.860
Their spells study clusters of stars, with
lesser spells like Glintstone Stars and Star

00:12:09.860 --> 00:12:16.630
Shower all echoing the great Stars of Ruin
spell that originally broke Master Lusat.

00:12:16.630 --> 00:12:21.190
Lusat and Azur were true masters at the academy,
after all.

00:12:21.190 --> 00:12:27.350
They were dubbed grand masters, specifically,
with special robes that reflected that - and

00:12:27.350 --> 00:12:32.730
it seems no one ever went on to achieve such
a rank, or sacrifice as much, as they did

00:12:32.730 --> 00:12:34.270
[Source: Azur's Glintstone Robe].

00:12:34.270 --> 00:12:35.490
And..they sacrificed a lot.

00:12:35.490 --> 00:12:40.680
They can barely even move any more - and when
Sellen talks about them, she talks about them

00:12:40.680 --> 00:12:45.080
being bodies, rather than a traditionally
living person.

00:12:45.080 --> 00:12:48.260
Perhaps they've ascended to a higher plane
of existence.

00:12:48.260 --> 00:12:54.230
Which would explain why they weren't really
around to form their own conspectus - something

00:12:54.230 --> 00:13:01.220
that was left to Karolos, and Olivinus, and
others, instead.

00:13:01.220 --> 00:13:05.470
---
With such enigmatic founders, many dedicated

00:13:05.470 --> 00:13:10.870
themselves to the study of glintstone with
vows of virtue and austerity.

00:13:10.870 --> 00:13:15.490
In return, they received the deep blue Robe
of Raya Lucaria [Source: Raya Lucaria], and

00:13:15.490 --> 00:13:18.350
were able to study on its grounds.

00:13:18.350 --> 00:13:24.470
Some nobles of Leyndell were even permitted
to study here - though their meagre accomplishments

00:13:24.470 --> 00:13:31.920
never warranted them earning a stone crown.

00:13:31.920 --> 00:13:38.630
To assist in their learning, a powerful spellcaster
would go and cast a spell called Terra Magica

00:13:38.630 --> 00:13:41.139
from the tallest belfry of the academy.

00:13:41.139 --> 00:13:42.820
Back then, this sigil was able to cover the
entire institution's grounds, and would be

00:13:42.820 --> 00:13:48.910
cast with such strength, and allow for such
a vivid experience of spell-casting success,

00:13:48.910 --> 00:13:53.800
that it turned "many a fledgling into a true
sorcerer in a flash of understanding" [Source:

00:13:53.800 --> 00:13:54.800
Terra Magica]

00:13:54.800 --> 00:13:57.430
But not all learning took place at the academy.

00:13:57.430 --> 00:14:02.270
In fact, a couple of signature spells were
specifically given to those who departed from

00:14:02.270 --> 00:14:05.600
the academy to embark on journeys.

00:14:05.600 --> 00:14:11.611
Starlight is a spell that guides sorcerers
in dark places, and it reads "Even during

00:14:11.611 --> 00:14:17.399
the blackest nights, sojourns underground,
or imprisonment in gaol, the stars are never

00:14:17.399 --> 00:14:19.579
far from a sorcerer's side."

00:14:19.579 --> 00:14:25.050
And then there was Glintstone Arc, which would
allow sorcerers to cleave through the ranks

00:14:25.050 --> 00:14:28.680
of the fools that would outnumber them, on
their journeys.

00:14:28.680 --> 00:14:33.930
Such journeys were encouraged by the academy
- there was even a conspectus for this practice,

00:14:33.930 --> 00:14:39.110
called the Hierodas Conspectus, with a crown
that was granted to scholars who engaged in

00:14:39.110 --> 00:14:42.500
nomadic study away from the academy [Source:
Hierodotas Glintstone Crown].

00:14:42.500 --> 00:14:48.290
In-game, this crown is worn by Errant Sorcerer
Wilhelm, who fights with night sorceries,

00:14:48.290 --> 00:14:52.210
and wields the staff of loss, which enhances
night sorceries.

00:14:52.210 --> 00:14:58.180
This staff doesn't even have a glintstone
embedded in its tip, and supposedly can only

00:14:58.180 --> 00:15:01.139
cast night sorceries as a result [Source:
Incorrect Staff of Loss Description].

00:15:01.139 --> 00:15:06.420
That's how important asceticism was to some
sorcerers, and they believed that it was a

00:15:06.420 --> 00:15:09.110
powerful path towards discovery.

00:15:09.110 --> 00:15:13.709
This conspectus also seemed to see value in
depriving the senses.

00:15:13.709 --> 00:15:17.029
The Crown of Hierodas is blindfolded, after
all.

00:15:17.029 --> 00:15:21.940
We see this same practice of veiling the eyes
down in the Eternal City as well, and the

00:15:21.940 --> 00:15:27.940
Nox's descendants were of course accomplished
practitioners of night sorceries, which seem

00:15:27.940 --> 00:15:35.540
to be thematically tied to this blindfolded,
ascetic embrace of the void.

00:15:35.540 --> 00:15:41.610
This habit of sending fledgling sorcerers
away must have posed a bit of a problem, however,

00:15:41.610 --> 00:15:47.279
[See: Thops], as when war broke out in the
Lands Between, Raya Lucaria would close and

00:15:47.279 --> 00:15:51.209
seal its gates, preventing access to all [Source:
Battlemage Robe].

00:15:51.209 --> 00:15:54.180
Including its journeying, fledgling sorcerers.

00:15:54.180 --> 00:15:59.600
The only way to get back inside, was to use
a glintstone key to activate the warp magic

00:15:59.600 --> 00:16:01.050
within the seals.

00:16:01.050 --> 00:16:06.280
These keys only seem to belong to accomplished
sorcerers - and they remember their users,

00:16:06.280 --> 00:16:10.980
meaning thieves, or bluntstones like Thops,
could not get inside.

00:16:10.980 --> 00:16:15.839
In the current age, Thops mentions that the
Academy closed its gates after declaring that

00:16:15.839 --> 00:16:19.020
"they wouldn't interfere with the Shattering".

00:16:19.020 --> 00:16:26.050
Now, this suggests to me that the Academy
had a habit of striving for a sort of neutrality

00:16:26.050 --> 00:16:28.649
or indifference in world affairs.

00:16:28.649 --> 00:16:34.610
Indeed, they had developed an entire Conspectus
who sought power in order to quell conflict

00:16:34.610 --> 00:16:35.610
[Source: Haima Glintstone Crown].

00:16:35.610 --> 00:16:41.920
These were the Battlemages of the Haima Conspectus,
who wielded stone clubs, and spells of cannon

00:16:41.920 --> 00:16:42.990
and gavel.

00:16:42.990 --> 00:16:47.740
A "gavel" is commonly used as a symbol of
judgement, and rather than interfering with

00:16:47.740 --> 00:16:54.060
outside affairs, I believe the Haima Conspectus
mainly functioned as the academy's judiciary.

00:16:54.060 --> 00:16:59.540
Their crown is even blindfolded, which is
widely regarded in the real world as a symbol

00:16:59.540 --> 00:17:01.111
of unbiased justice.

00:17:01.111 --> 00:17:02.220
[Source: Lady of Justice Statue].

00:17:02.220 --> 00:17:07.620
With their preparedness for combat, the Haima
Conspectus were cited as being "the only ones

00:17:07.620 --> 00:17:11.890
who dared to venture outside whenever war
had broken out".

00:17:11.890 --> 00:17:17.220
And just like the blindfolded members of the
Hierodas Conspectus, the Battlemages of Haima

00:17:17.220 --> 00:17:22.400
believed that seclusion was "no way to foster
discovery", and instead believed that it was

00:17:22.400 --> 00:17:25.660
"only a convenient form of escape" [Source:
Battlemage Robe].

00:17:25.660 --> 00:17:31.430
That said, we do find sorcerers of other conspectus'
outside the Academy as well.

00:17:31.430 --> 00:17:35.891
Though you can sort of infer that they're
a bit wary to be away from home..because they're

00:17:35.891 --> 00:17:38.400
often accompanied by Marionettes.

00:17:38.400 --> 00:17:44.240
The Marionettes are dolls - constructs that
were crafted and animated by the sorcerers,

00:17:44.240 --> 00:17:45.550
who are their masters.

00:17:45.550 --> 00:17:51.410
There are a couple of variants - an avian
variant with curved swords that can fly and

00:17:51.410 --> 00:17:58.920
throw fire pots, and the typical marionettes
with spiked spears, short swords, and shortbows.

00:17:58.920 --> 00:18:00.690
Lots of shortbows.

00:18:00.690 --> 00:18:05.660
These will commonly drop down upon you in
ambush, and while they like to go a bit ballistic,

00:18:05.660 --> 00:18:12.530
they do act as crudely effective support for
a ton of the sorcerers that you'll meet in-game.

00:18:12.530 --> 00:18:17.520
You'll even find a few of these down in the
Raya Lucaria Crystal Tunnel, where glintstone

00:18:17.520 --> 00:18:21.630
miners are hard at work extracting glintstone,
and ore.

00:18:21.630 --> 00:18:26.850
These miners don't use conventional tools
though - instead, they mine with a Digger's

00:18:26.850 --> 00:18:32.970
Staff, embedded with a glintstone, casting
spells such as "Shatter Earth" or "Rock Blaster".

00:18:32.970 --> 00:18:37.470
A fascinating little detail here though, is
that these mining spells carried enormous

00:18:37.470 --> 00:18:41.760
stigma at the academy [Source: Shatter Earth],
because they marked their user as a failed

00:18:41.760 --> 00:18:47.300
scholar..perhaps as someone who had to turn
to menial labour - lacking the intelligence

00:18:47.300 --> 00:18:51.070
to pursue the complex mysteries of the cosmos.

00:18:51.070 --> 00:18:57.390
Indeed, the overseers attack by crushing scraps
of glintstone, rather than with any advanced

00:18:57.390 --> 00:18:58.390
sorceries.

00:18:58.390 --> 00:19:04.440
At the end of the Crystal Tunnel is a Crystalian,
an inorganic being that was hewn from crystal

00:19:04.440 --> 00:19:05.500
long ago [Source: Crystalian Spirit Ashes].

00:19:05.500 --> 00:19:07.830
But these are more than mere constructs.

00:19:07.830 --> 00:19:14.340
They are ancient, and even possess a faint
sort of intellect dubbed the "wisdom of the

00:19:14.340 --> 00:19:15.340
stone".

00:19:15.340 --> 00:19:20.620
Long ago, they even made a "concord", or agreement,
with the Carian Royal Family.

00:19:20.620 --> 00:19:26.190
We don't know the nature of this agreement,
but some can be found chilling upon the moonlight

00:19:26.190 --> 00:19:38.900
altar, and we know that they did teach the
Carians a spell called Magic Downpour, to

00:19:38.900 --> 00:19:40.650
mark the occassion.

00:19:40.650 --> 00:19:44.050
And Raya Lucaria sought kinship with these
beings as well.

00:19:44.050 --> 00:19:50.059
For they are "close to the ideals of the primeval
current, and so are revered guests of the

00:19:50.059 --> 00:19:51.059
sorcerers" [Source: Shattering Crystal].

00:19:51.059 --> 00:19:55.690
The best example of this might be down in
the dimly lit Academy Crystal Cave underneath

00:19:55.690 --> 00:20:02.049
Raya Lucaria - a crystal cave that is not
mined - perhaps out of respect for the Crystalian

00:20:02.049 --> 00:20:03.630
Duo at the end.

00:20:03.630 --> 00:20:10.010
There are even living quarters down here - and
I suspect these belong to a group of sorcerers

00:20:10.010 --> 00:20:16.659
called the "Crystal Cadre", which was founded
to research the wisdom of stone possessed

00:20:16.659 --> 00:20:18.179
by the Crystalian.

00:20:18.179 --> 00:20:23.660
However, just like the primeval current, the
sorcerers clearly don't have all the answers

00:20:23.660 --> 00:20:25.010
on these beings.

00:20:25.010 --> 00:20:30.669
They call them "inscrutiable", and note that
they have "but one clear purpose; and that

00:20:30.669 --> 00:20:33.950
is to safeguard their crystals unto the end".

00:20:33.950 --> 00:20:38.520
Though there is one theory on these beings
- and it's that they are waiting - yearning

00:20:38.520 --> 00:20:43.419
"for the return of their creator who will
carve for them new brethren" [Source: Crystal

00:20:43.419 --> 00:20:44.419
Weapons].

00:20:44.419 --> 00:20:48.770
A few sorcerers down here researching the
Crystalian are in possession of the Twinsage

00:20:48.770 --> 00:20:53.860
Helm, which marks them as members of the Twinsage
Conspectus.

00:20:53.860 --> 00:21:00.299
These were the elites of the academy, "permitted
to study and excel in sorceries of all kinds"

00:21:00.299 --> 00:21:06.990
- and I assume it was these members who would
climb out of this cave, and cast the legendary

00:21:06.990 --> 00:21:10.580
Terra Magica, that would cover the entire
academy's grounds.

00:21:10.580 --> 00:21:19.409
But the Twinsage helm wasn't the only mark
of a proficient scholar - there was also the

00:21:19.409 --> 00:21:24.610
Witch's Glintstone Crown which was "granted
to a scholar who excelled in her studies,

00:21:24.610 --> 00:21:27.950
which also merited the title of witch".

00:21:27.950 --> 00:21:33.060
And again - you can see most of these Conspectus
portraits hanging in Raya Lucaria.

00:21:33.060 --> 00:21:35.470
For example, here is The Witch.

00:21:35.470 --> 00:21:36.789
The Twinsage.

00:21:36.789 --> 00:21:42.909
Karolos, Olivinus..Lazuli?..all of these portraits
are hung in the Debate Parlor of the Academy,

00:21:42.909 --> 00:21:47.980
where members would likely have engaged in
argument in order to test and help validate

00:21:47.980 --> 00:21:49.410
their ideas.

00:21:49.410 --> 00:21:55.059
It's also where I assume they argued whether
certain things even should be allowed to be

00:21:55.059 --> 00:21:58.450
learned, or whether certain members should
be exiled.

00:21:58.450 --> 00:22:02.169
But we'll get to that shortly.

00:22:02.169 --> 00:22:06.960
The final conspectus we haven't yet mentioned
is the Lazuli Conspectus.

00:22:06.960 --> 00:22:13.180
These sorcerers studied lunar sorceries - A
quote unquote "Heterodox pursuit that views

00:22:13.180 --> 00:22:18.580
the moon as equal to the stars"..with a robe
coloured "in the hue of the full moon which

00:22:18.580 --> 00:22:20.789
signifies their heresy".

00:22:20.789 --> 00:22:24.990
And of course, these sorceries include many
signature spells of Caria [Note: You could

00:22:24.990 --> 00:22:27.559
probably argue that the Lazuli conspectus
also showed up after Rennala was ousted from

00:22:27.559 --> 00:22:28.559
Raya Lucaria].

00:22:28.559 --> 00:22:34.110
This is Carian Manor, and to the south are
the stargazing rounds - both situated upon

00:22:34.110 --> 00:22:39.970
the western coast of Liurnia - which, according
to the map, has always been closely associated

00:22:39.970 --> 00:22:41.970
with Carian Royalty [Source: Map: Liurnia,
West].

00:22:41.970 --> 00:22:44.130
They have been around for a long time.

00:22:44.130 --> 00:22:46.000
A really long time.

00:22:46.000 --> 00:22:51.510
Specifically, Caria traces its roots all the
way back to the ancient astrologers that existed

00:22:51.510 --> 00:22:53.659
alongside the fire giants.

00:22:53.659 --> 00:22:58.640
This is most apparent when looking at two
items - first the Sword of Night and Flame,

00:22:58.640 --> 00:23:02.630
which became a "storied sword and treasure
of Caria Manor".

00:23:02.630 --> 00:23:08.500
It was clearly crafted to commemorate the
astrologers early experiences with the primeval

00:23:08.500 --> 00:23:13.570
current...and their shared experience with
the Fire Giants, as well.. and the fact that

00:23:13.570 --> 00:23:19.789
Caria inherited this sword suggests that they
trace their ancestry back to the time of this

00:23:19.789 --> 00:23:20.789
sword.

00:23:20.789 --> 00:23:25.970
And then there's the Stargazer Heirloom, which
tells of the rise of Caria as a house of royalty

00:23:25.970 --> 00:23:28.290
through Rennala, and herfull moon.

00:23:28.290 --> 00:23:31.880
"The young astrologer gazed at the night sky
as she walked.

00:23:31.880 --> 00:23:35.400
She had always chased the stars every step
of her journey.

00:23:35.400 --> 00:23:40.919
Then she met the full moon — and, in time,
the astrologer became a queen".

00:23:40.919 --> 00:23:45.780
This royal house continued this tradition
of stargazing, and raised princesses, and

00:23:45.780 --> 00:23:49.169
Carian Knights to serve as their retainers.

00:23:49.169 --> 00:23:54.070
One of the foremost Carian Knights was named
Loretta - a woman we talked about more in

00:23:54.070 --> 00:23:59.330
the recent video on the Eternal Cities, as
it was rumoured that she was an albinauric.

00:23:59.330 --> 00:24:05.789
Albinaurics, as you may know - were widely
despised in the Lands Between - though Caria

00:24:05.789 --> 00:24:10.390
is one of the few factions that seems friendly
with them.

00:24:10.390 --> 00:24:16.799
Albinauric sorcerers are found all throughout
Caria Manor, and one, named Pidia - is literally

00:24:16.799 --> 00:24:25.039
called a "Carian Servant", linking the Eternal
Cities with Caria, in an alliance which perhaps

00:24:25.039 --> 00:24:28.970
allowed them to learn more about the stars
[See: the Weathered Map that Pidia gives you.

00:24:28.970 --> 00:24:30.640
It shows where to find Amber Starlight, used
to make Starlight Draughts.]

00:24:30.640 --> 00:24:34.920
And Rennala, with her full moon sorceries,
was their champion.

00:24:34.920 --> 00:24:37.610
A prominent one too , apparently [Source:
Remembrance of the Full Moon Queen].

00:24:37.610 --> 00:24:41.809
And it's no surprise when you look at the
powerful characteristics of her full moon

00:24:41.809 --> 00:24:46.419
- it has immense gravity, and eclipses all
other magics.

00:24:46.419 --> 00:24:47.919
It lowers defenses.

00:24:47.919 --> 00:24:53.870
It is "enchanting", and Rennala used all of
these traits, to charm the Academy [Source:

00:24:53.870 --> 00:24:59.110
Remembrance], to "bewitch them", and become
not just the Queen of Caria - but also the

00:24:59.110 --> 00:25:01.929
master of Raya Lucaria itself.

00:25:01.929 --> 00:25:07.720
And so, of course, here is her portrait, displayed
most prominently in the Academy of Raya Lucaria...

00:25:07.720 --> 00:25:08.720
---

00:25:08.720 --> 00:25:12.330
Right next to what many assume, is a portrait
of Sellen.

00:25:12.330 --> 00:25:17.350
For if you unmask her in-game..then she actually
looks very similar, to this witch.

00:25:17.350 --> 00:25:18.350
[Source: Prizzaa Gaming Channel].

00:25:18.350 --> 00:25:25.029
Someone who was worthy of an entire conspectus,
and apparently, was the most promising sorceress

00:25:25.029 --> 00:25:27.799
in the history of the academy [Source: Thops].

00:25:27.799 --> 00:25:35.700
But even Sellen, with all her promise, would
not be tolerated, in the end.

00:25:35.700 --> 00:25:39.830
If you recall, I was exiled from the Academy
of Raya Lucaria.

00:25:39.830 --> 00:25:45.810
It was for attempting to restore the primeval
current of glintstone sorcery.

00:25:45.810 --> 00:25:51.299
The toothless pedantry peddled by the Carian
royal family can rot for all I care.

00:25:51.299 --> 00:25:56.970
I want glintstone sorceries that open our
minds, unbound by terrestrial taboos.

00:25:56.970 --> 00:25:58.429
No matter what we give in return.

00:25:58.429 --> 00:26:04.100
For Sellen to know so much about what she
calls "toothless pedantry peddled by the Carian

00:26:04.100 --> 00:26:08.750
Royal Family", I assume she was a part of
the academy during Rennala's reign over it

00:26:08.750 --> 00:26:14.120
- and that it was Rennala's influence that
finally led to the Academy's intolerance of

00:26:14.120 --> 00:26:16.490
primeval current research.

00:26:16.490 --> 00:26:19.690
And Sellen wasn't the only one expelled from
the academy.

00:26:19.690 --> 00:26:25.559
The masters Azur and Lusat - two of the founding
masters of glintstone sorcery, were at some

00:26:25.559 --> 00:26:28.730
point driven from the academy, as well [Source:
Sellen's Dialogue].

00:26:28.730 --> 00:26:30.190
And it's easy to see why.

00:26:30.190 --> 00:26:33.080
The primeval current is dangerous.

00:26:33.080 --> 00:26:36.500
Lusat's mind was broken after watching a star
cluster break apart.

00:26:36.500 --> 00:26:42.929
Azur saw a darkness in the primeval current,
and was left fearful of its abyss.

00:26:42.929 --> 00:26:49.340
Imagine something so dangerous that just looking
at it can damage your mind..

00:26:49.340 --> 00:26:54.400
In this way the primeval current is almost
Lovecraftian in its horror - we can't pin

00:26:54.400 --> 00:27:00.840
down the exact truth of why it terrifies,
but we see its terrible effects on others,

00:27:00.840 --> 00:27:02.299
and are left to wonder.

00:27:02.299 --> 00:27:05.640
What's more...this cosmic current is primeval.

00:27:05.640 --> 00:27:10.220
It's one of the first, if not the first thing
to exist in the universe.

00:27:10.220 --> 00:27:16.240
The fact that our cosmic origins might be
terrifying, really is a kind of bizarre and

00:27:16.240 --> 00:27:24.360
bewitching thought, right?

00:27:24.360 --> 00:27:40.370
But Raya Lucaria was an institution now, with
power, and influence in the Lands Between,

00:27:40.370 --> 00:27:44.590
and with those things, naturally, would have
come a need for self-preservation.

00:27:44.590 --> 00:27:49.600
And the biggest threat at this stage wouldn't
have been external..it would have been internal.

00:27:49.600 --> 00:27:53.820
The biggest threat was probing the primeval
current too deeply.

00:27:53.820 --> 00:28:09.620
And so, the masters Azur and Lusat were eventually
driven from the Academy, as was Sellen the

00:28:09.620 --> 00:28:10.620
Witch.

00:28:10.620 --> 00:28:15.380
When we first meet her, Sellen states that
glintstone sorcery is rooted in the study

00:28:15.380 --> 00:28:21.269
of the stars, and that most sorcerers these
days have forgotten this fact.

00:28:21.269 --> 00:28:26.700
She resents that the sorcerers took their
power, then turned a blind eye to deeper research

00:28:26.700 --> 00:28:29.400
in order to protect themselves.

00:28:29.400 --> 00:28:34.000
It's kind of easy to empathise with her, and
to see her as this underdog..fighting for

00:28:34.000 --> 00:28:40.309
the truth against an enormous institution
-

00:28:40.309 --> 00:28:47.100
But can you really blame Raya Lucaria for
taking a stand, when you see this?

00:28:47.100 --> 00:28:49.510
This is a School of Graven Mages.

00:28:49.510 --> 00:28:54.440
A mass of sorcerers, fused together so that
they might be fashioned into the seeds of

00:28:54.440 --> 00:28:55.440
stars.

00:28:55.440 --> 00:28:56.440
[Source: Graven-School/Mass Talisman].

00:28:56.440 --> 00:29:00.299
As the lore goes, this was apparently a valid
line of research into the primeval current,

00:29:00.299 --> 00:29:05.850
and that, in the name of that research, fellow
sorcerers should be "collected", and fused

00:29:05.850 --> 00:29:11.550
together in a cluster.

00:29:11.550 --> 00:29:19.370
These creations were considered "the nightmare
of the academy", representing Sellen's complete

00:29:19.370 --> 00:29:23.830
loyalty to the truth, no matter the cost to
her fellow man.

00:29:23.830 --> 00:29:30.070
Naturally, such a thing had to be forbidden..but
then, it's ironic isn't it?

00:29:30.070 --> 00:29:37.330
That the exactly line of enquiry that gave
rise to the academy, was the very thing that

00:29:37.330 --> 00:30:34.990
posed a threat to 

00:30:34.990 --> 00:31:45.870
its existence, in 

00:31:45.870 --> 00:32:00.060
the end?

00:32:00.060 --> 00:32:01.060
---

00:32:01.060 --> 00:32:02.060
---

00:32:02.060 --> 00:32:47.940
And 
it 

00:32:47.940 --> 00:32:50.750
was then, that those at the academy realized.

00:32:50.750 --> 00:32:52.830
That Rennala was no champion, after all.

00:32:52.830 --> 00:32:53.850
[Source: Queen's Set].

00:32:53.850 --> 00:33:00.900
When we see her, we realise that she was likely
left quite witless and inate after this event,

00:33:00.900 --> 00:33:06.780
and so it was no surprise that the Academy
took this chance to rebel against the Carian

00:33:06.780 --> 00:33:07.780
Royals [Source: Miriel's Dialogue].

00:33:07.780 --> 00:33:08.780
---

00:33:08.780 --> 00:33:12.610
With Rennala essentially held hostage and
safely locked in their Grand Library, the

00:33:12.610 --> 00:33:17.340
academy went to war with Caria - focusing
their assault upon Caria Manor, for that is

00:33:17.340 --> 00:33:21.909
where a siege, commemorated by this graveyard
of swords, took place.

00:33:21.909 --> 00:33:26.850
The enchanted soldiers who fought on behalf
of the Academy were named the Knights of the

00:33:26.850 --> 00:33:27.880
Cuckoo.

00:33:27.880 --> 00:33:33.019
Wearing red and blue surcoats that depict
their namesake, and carrying shields that

00:33:33.019 --> 00:33:39.120
boasted high magic damage negation - they
were explicitly purposed as "mage hunters",

00:33:39.120 --> 00:33:43.840
and have been quoted as stating "our enemy
is none other than Caria itself" [Source:

00:33:43.840 --> 00:33:44.840
Cuckoo Greatshield].

00:33:44.840 --> 00:33:50.660
They also throw Albinauric Pots, which reference
their torture [Note: The Albinauric Pot features

00:33:50.660 --> 00:33:55.360
a Black Dumpling - a torturous headpiece]
and hatred of the albinaurics, who, again,

00:33:55.360 --> 00:34:01.269
are found all throughout Caria.

00:34:01.269 --> 00:34:06.549
But despite some of their descriptions saying
that the Cuckoo Knights were "sworn to the

00:34:06.549 --> 00:34:10.310
academy" [Source: Cuckoo Greatshield], I think
that's actually just wishful thinking by Raya

00:34:10.310 --> 00:34:11.310
Lucaria.

00:34:11.310 --> 00:34:15.631
The Scholar's Armament/Shield spells, for
example, were actually spells that were, quote

00:34:15.631 --> 00:34:20.070
unquote, "taught to the Knights of the Cuckoo
as payment for their contract".

00:34:20.070 --> 00:34:23.389
So..they were getting paid to fight.

00:34:23.389 --> 00:34:28.169
And learning these low-intellect spells suited
them, because they were NOT proficient sorcerers

00:34:28.169 --> 00:34:33.530
- for example, instead of casting spells,
they would crush broken clumps of glintstone,

00:34:33.530 --> 00:34:37.940
dubbed "faux sorceries", or fake sorceries,
by the academy.

00:34:37.940 --> 00:34:43.139
But perhaps most telling about their loyalty
is the Cuckoo Knight Armor, which says "Its

00:34:43.139 --> 00:34:48.990
left breast is emblazoned with a peering cuckoo,
whence came their name", straight up admits

00:34:48.990 --> 00:34:55.329
that "perhaps the bird's shrewd gaze is an
expression of their refusal to be mere servants

00:34:55.329 --> 00:34:56.379
of the Academy".

00:34:56.379 --> 00:35:00.500
Anyway, whatever the case, the Knights of
the Cuckoo failed pretty hard.

00:35:00.500 --> 00:35:04.970
They were not only defeated in the siege of
Caria manor - but they were turned into puppets

00:35:04.970 --> 00:35:08.650
there, and many now fight on Caria's behalf.

00:35:08.650 --> 00:35:14.810
We get an idea of how much they must resent
this - when they somehow break free and confront

00:35:14.810 --> 00:35:18.920
Pidia - a Carian, an albinauric, and a mage.

00:35:18.920 --> 00:36:08.539
Three things that they absolutely hate.

